{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\na = [int(i) for i in input().split()]\nleft = a[:n // 2]\nright = a[n // 2:]\n\ndef generate(part):\n    res = []\n\n    def dfs(pos, total):\n        if pos == len(part):\n            res.append(total % m)\n            return\n        dfs(pos + 1, total)\n        dfs(pos + 1, total + part[pos])\n\n    dfs(0, 0)\n    return res\n\ns1 = generate(left)\ns2 = generate(right)\ns1.sort()\ns2.sort()\n\ndef largest_less_than(lst, x):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(lst) - 1\n    ans = 0\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if lst[mid] < x:\n            ans = lst[mid]\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1\n    return ans\n\nbest = 0\nfor i in s1:\n    cur = (i + largest_less_than(s2, m - i)) % m\n    if cur > best:\n        best = cur\nprint(best)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdint>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid generate_sums(const vector<int>& part, int m, vector<int>& res) {\n    int len = part.size();\n    // Use recursion to generate all subset sums modulo m\n    function<void(int, int64_t)> dfs = [&](int pos, int64_t total) {\n        if (pos == len) {\n            res.push_back(total % m);\n            return;\n        }\n        dfs(pos + 1, total);\n        dfs(pos + 1, total + part[pos]);\n    };\n    dfs(0, 0);\n}\n\nint largest_less_than(const vector<int>& lst, int x) {\n    // Find largest element < x in sorted list\n    int lo = 0, hi = (int)lst.size() - 1;\n    int ans = 0;\n    while (lo <= hi) {\n        int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;\n        if (lst[mid] < x) {\n            ans = lst[mid];\n            lo = mid + 1;\n        } else {\n            hi = mid - 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        cin >> a[i];\n    }\n\n    vector<int> left(a.begin(), a.begin() + n / 2);\n    vector<int> right(a.begin() + n / 2, a.end());\n\n    vector<int> s1, s2;\n    generate_sums(left, m, s1);\n    generate_sums(right, m, s2);\n\n    sort(s1.begin(), s1.end());\n    sort(s2.begin(), s2.end());\n\n    int best = 0;\n    for (int i : s1) {\n        int cur = (i + largest_less_than(s2, m - i)) % m;\n        if (cur > best) best = cur;\n    }\n    cout << best << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.99\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.9141146923357155e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00010632903286023065, -7.748303323751315e-05, -3.933898824470816e-06, -0.04863150045275688, -1.2993727978027891e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -2.169585604860913e-05, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.004089921247214079, -0.004080779384821653, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.001191025716252625, -0.0044434149749577045, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.31337806582450867, -0.00175405596